  the DRAT gate was shown to reject non-refutations before being relied on;
  the 19 MB of gitignored CNFs regenerate byte-identically;
  the A7 evidence reproduces (20/20 CNFs, 15/15 DRAT refutations, 5/5 models);
  Implementation B independently reproduces the same 225 triples.

Note what this does NOT establish.  f(7,7) = 38 is not a Lean theorem.
As of 2026-09-17 the upper bound no longer rests on any published lemma:
RealUpperBound.isGreatest_38_real proves that 38 is exactly the greatest
number of boundary intersection points of two simple heptagons with REAL
coordinates, as a set in R x R, importing nothing.  What it carries is ONE
hypothesis -- general position, a field of RConfig.  Discharging that is
AKR section 9 plus section 3's unproved clause, and neither is formalized.
And no person outside this AI-assisted process has reviewed any of it.
See docs/verification-status.md rows 4, 18, 46, 47.
